{"title":"Quantum API","sub":"Leave the cloud? Only partly.","type":"Cost & operations","industry":"Software","geo":"United States","diff":2,"fmt":"Candidate-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Make vs buy · total cost of ownership · peak vs average load","prompt":"Quantum runs payment APIs for online shops. Its cloud bill is $14M a year and growing 25% a year with the business. The CTO proposes moving everything onto servers Quantum owns, in rented data-centre space, saying it would halve the bill. The CFO asks you to test it over the next four years.","clarify":[{"q":"What runs on the cloud?","a":"About 60% is steady traffic that runs all day. 40% is spiky: big sales days and batch jobs, sometimes 5× normal load for a few hours."},{"q":"Cost to move steady work?","a":"$12M of servers, sized for year-4 volume and lasting four years, plus $2M to migrate. Then $1.8M a year for space and power, and 8 engineers at $180k each."},{"q":"Cost to move spiky work too?","a":"Owned servers would have to be sized for year-4 peaks: another $24M of servers, $1M to migrate, $1.6M a year of space and power, 4 more engineers."},{"q":"Anything else?","a":"Ignore resale value of servers after four years."}],"structure":{"root":"Should Quantum move off the cloud, and how much of it?","branches":[{"head":"Workloads","items":["Steady vs spiky","Growth"]},{"head":"Cost of each option","items":["Cloud bill","Servers, migration","Space, power, engineers"]},{"head":"Risks","items":["Reliability","Engineering distraction","Peak capacity"]}]},"hypothesis":"Owning servers is cheap for steady load but expensive for peaks, because you pay for peak capacity all year. I expect moving only the steady part to win.","questions":[{"q":"Here is the projected cloud bill. What would it cost over four years to stay on the cloud?","exhibit":{"kind":"table","headers":["","Total bill ($M)","Steady 60%","Spiky 40%"],"rows":[["Year 1","14.0","8.4","5.6"],["Year 2","17.5","10.5","7.0"],["Year 3","21.9","13.1","8.8"],["Year 4","27.3","16.4","10.9"],["Total","80.7","48.4","32.3"]],"title":"Exhibit 1 · Cloud bill at 25% growth a year","note":null,"align":["l","r","r","r"],"boldLast":true},"answer":"<p>Four-year cloud bill: <b>$80.7M</b>.</p>"},{"q":"Compare: move only the steady work (hybrid), or move everything.","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"393.86pt\" height=\"164.94pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 393.86 164.94\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 164.94 L 393.86 164.94 L 393.86 0 L 0 0 L 0 164.94 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 40.7 139.04 L 386.66 139.04 L 386.66 11.528 L 40.7 11.528 L 40.7 139.04 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"><g id=\"xtick_1\"><g id=\"line2d_1\"><defs><path id=\"ma99844d2ee\" d=\"M 0 0 L 0 3.5 \" style=\"stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></defs><g><use xlink:href=\"#ma99844d2ee\" x=\"101.355325\" y=\"139.04\" style=\"fill: #4a5568; stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g style=\"fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(74.162668 155.265) scale(0.09 -0.09)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-30\" d=\"M 1850 -77 Q 1312 -77 925 131 Q 538 339 269 704 L 666 1037 Q 902 723 1190 560 Q 1478 397 1869 397 Q 2349 397 2601 627 Q 2854 858 2854 1242 Q 2854 1453 2771 1600 Q 2688 1747 2505 1846 Q 2323 1946 2029 2010 L 1664 2093 Q 1261 2189 979 2342 Q 698 2496 550 2739 Q 403 2982 403 3322 Q 403 3718 588 3990 Q 774 4262 1110 4403 Q 1446 4544 1882 4544 Q 2387 4544 2748 4358 Q 3110 4173 3360 3814 L 2957 3520 Q 2778 3776 2512 3923 Q 2246 4070 1856 4070 Q 1427 4070 1180 3884 Q 934 3699 934 3341 Q 934 3130 1027 2989 Q 1120 2848 1305 2755 Q 1491 2662 1773 2598 L 2138 2515 Q 2573 2419 2848 2252 Q 3123 2086 3254 1843 Q 3386 1600 3386 1267 Q 3386 858 3200 557 Q 3014 256 